 "ambiguities": [
  "Matching keys: k2 is the sum of readout_grid_mev as the registration says (not the file value edep_scintillator_mev used as the energy key in EXP-015); k1 is the count of readout cells with a positive deposit.",
  "Standardisation: logs of the two keys, then mean and population standard deviation (ddof = 0) over ALL fiducial events of both classes with a positive cell count and energy, before cut (a) is applied (the registration says 'pooled fiducial events').",
  "Common support: 'within 0.25 standardised units in BOTH keys' is read as Chebyshev distance <= 0.25 (inclusive) to at least one event of the other class that also passes (a); it is evaluated once, not iterated.",
  "Fold seed: the stratified split of repeat r uses random_state = 20261109 + r; the HistGradientBoosting random_state of fold f of repeat r is 20261109 + 5 r + f (immaterial: no early stopping and fewer than 2e5 rows, so it is not used).",
  "Class-balanced sample weights are computed on the training fold only (sklearn 'balanced') and are also given to the logistic regression (the registration is silent on its weights); the standardiser is fitted on the training fold only.",
  "Nadeau-Bengio ratio n_test/n_train: the ratio of the mean actual test size to the mean actual training size over the 100 folds (about 0.25); s^2 is the sample variance (ddof = 1) of the 100 deltas; the interval is two-sided 95 % with t on 99 degrees of freedom, and the decision rule uses that interval's limits.",
  "Negative control: all 18 multiscale columns are permuted jointly (one row permutation per repeat, generator default_rng([20261109, 18, r])) over the events of the hard subset and reused by all five folds of the repeat. The registration names 'invalid' only for an upper limit below 0; an interval that excludes 0 on the worse side is reported as 'not passed' (the control 'must contain 0'), and the primary result is then not to be read.",
  "Same-class null: uses the hard-subset electrons (not all fiducial electrons); one stratified 5-fold cross-fit per repeat (fold seed 20261109 + 1000 + r, random balanced split generator default_rng([20261109, 19, r])); the AUC is that of the pooled out-of-fold scores; the standard error is the Hanley-McNeil null value sqrt((n1 + n2 + 1) / (12 n1 n2)); the check passes when every repeat of both models lies within 0.5 +- 3 SE (the mean over the repeats is also reported).",
  "AUC difference and the protons passing at 90 % electron efficiency use, for every repeat, the pooled out-of-fold scores of that repeat; the threshold is the order statistic of rejection_limits.electron_threshold on those electron scores (protons never enter it). Summaries are the mean and range over the 20 repeats (the repeats reuse the same events, so they are not independent); the Clopper-Pearson one-sided 95 % limit is reported per repeat for k = 0.",
  "theta <= 12 deg: the stratum is taken within the hard subset as defined (standardisation and common support are not recomputed within the stratum); the test is run only if both classes keep >= 100 events.",
  "Full fiducial sample: all fiducial electrons and truth-interacting protons, with the registered per-window eligibility masking of the multiscale features (NaN below 336 / 572 occupied cells), handled by the native NaN support of HistGradientBoosting; missingness can leak class information (found in the S0 audit), so this secondary view is expected to be trivially separable and says nothing about the multiscale features. The logistic model is not run on it (it needs imputation).",
  "Secondary logistic model: same hard subset, same folds and weights as the primary HistGradientBoosting comparison.",
  "Ablations (C + D0 only, C + D1 and D2 only): same folds as the primary; descriptive, interval reported with the same Nadeau-Bengio formula but no decision.",
  "Figure 2 shows the out-of-fold scores of repeat 0 only (log-odds axis), with that repeat's 90 % electron-efficiency threshold."
 ],
